// Review reported: 6 diagnostics. Verdict: "good" -- bounded, no
// explosion.
//
// Reconstruction: approximate by necessity (no positions or specific
// mistakes are given to reconstruct against), but count-faithful. The 4
// lines of this program's body combine a reserved word used as a
// parameter name (`per`), a missing `;`, a `)` where `]` was required, and
// a symbolic `<` where `lt` was required, plus one stray trailing `}` --
// six distinct grammar violations across four content lines. Verified
// against e5f283d: exactly 6 diagnostics, the compiler exits 1 without
